I would like to announce my candidacy for the OpenStack Technical Committee.

I have been involved with OpenStack since the Kilo release as a user,
operator and developer, deploying and operating multiple OpenStack cloud
environments.

I am a core reviewer and release liaison for the Kolla and Kolla-Ansible
projects. My main area of expertise is cloud infrastructure and its
deployment, especially networking with OVN, and compute with Nova and Ironic.
Recently, I have also been working on improving aarch64 support across
various OpenStack projects. I have presented my work and experience at
several conferences, including OpenInfra Summits.

If elected, I would like to contribute my broad technical experience to the
TC. In particular, I would like to promote better aarch64 support across
OpenStack, including wider CI coverage. This will require coordination between
OpenStack projects, OpenDev and hardware vendors. I would like to help with
that work.

Affiliation: StackHPC Ltd
